# The AOSP list pads about 1.1 million entries with generated forms at
# frequency 1; build-dict.py keeps entries from 74 up (about 645,000,
# real definite forms such as franceza included), and find-supplement.py
# adds back the rarer ones in use.
min-freq 74
# Little text: a word in both sources 10 times in all is enough (niciuna).
supplement-min-total 10

# The cedilla letters of older keyboards stand for the comma-below ones of
# the list (aşa -> așa).
ş ș
ţ ț

# find-respellings.py: â inside a word was written î until 1993 (cînd,
# sînt: când, sunt); the list has the current forms. Only lowercase words
# (after a prefix î stays: neînțeles; the corpus decides).
respell (?<=[a-zăâîșțşţ])î(?=[a-zăâîșțşţ]) â lower list
